> What's CVS?
Concurrent Versions System.

> And what's it used on and for, generally?
The main use for CVS is storing text files, along with logs of changes
which were made to them, when, by whom, and why. It also provides a
way to roll back such changes if necessary, or to look at an older
version. http://www.cvshome.org is probably the place to look for
more details.

